    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nNeovim handles four of the LSP workspace refresh requests:\n- `workspace/codeLens/refresh`\n- `workspace/diagnostic/refresh`\n- `workspace/inlayHint/refresh`\n- `workspace/semanticTokens/refresh`\n\n`workspace/foldingRange/refresh` (LSP 3.18) is missing, even though Neovim has a full folding range implementation (`vim.lsp.foldexpr()`). The method is already present in the generated protocol tables (`protocol.Methods.workspace_foldingRange_refresh`), and the generated meta types already include `lsp.FoldingRangeWorkspaceClientCapabilities.refreshSupport` - only the client-side wiring is absent.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNeovim advertises `workspace.foldingRange.refreshSupport = true` and, on receiving `workspace/foldingRange/refresh` from a client, re-requests `textDocument/foldingRange` for that client in every attached buffer with an active folding range state, then updates folds - mirroring how `vim.lsp.inlay_hint.on_refresh()` handles `workspace/inlayHint/refresh`.",
